# User Help File Maintenance

## Rule

Whenever a change affects how the user interacts with the app — new features, changed workflows, renamed actions, removed options, or modified UI behaviour — update `src/help.md` as part of the same task.

## What counts as a user-facing change

- New screens, dialogs, or controls
- Changed labels, menu items, or button actions
- Modified or removed settings/options
- Changed keyboard shortcuts or gestures
- New or removed export/import formats
- Behavioural changes that affect the outcome of a user action

## What does not require an update

- Internal refactors with no visible effect
- Bug fixes that restore already-documented behaviour
- Style/layout tweaks that do not change how the app is used

## How to apply

1. Identify which section(s) of `src/help.md` describe the affected feature.
2. Edit those sections to reflect the new behaviour. Add a new section if the feature is entirely new.
3. Do not add a "Changed in vX.Y" callout unless the user asks for it — keep the help text current and authoritative, not a changelog.
4. Leave `<!-- LOAD_EXAMPLES_BUTTON -->` in place — `HelpDialog.tsx` renders the load-examples button at that marker.
5. Use raw HTML only for blocks that Markdown cannot express (e.g. the nested-list example). Keep button labels and other interactive UI in React, not in the markdown file.
